        {
          "id": "the_four_blocks_select_the_same_cohorts_and_emit_different_ones",
          "description": "THE ASSERTION THIS FIXTURE EXISTS FOR. All four pollutant-processes SELECT the same 125 candidates -- `pollutantprocessmappedmodelyear` covers model years 1950-2060 for every one of them, so `pp_selectedCohortCount` is 125 four times and `run_cohortSelectionTotal` is 500. What they EMIT differs: 124 for total NOx, because `emissionratebyage` has no fuel-type-9 / ageGroup-2099 row and the model year 2000 electricity cohort therefore finds no rate; and 104 for each species, because `nono2ratio` has no fuel type 9 row at all. 124 + 3 x 104 = 436, which is `n_outputRate`, recomputed here from the mask rather than trusted -- and the prefix count's last value is the same 436 by a different route. 312 of the 436 arrive through the chain.\\n\\n`process-brakewear` had these two numbers EQUAL for every block, which is what let it divide an output row number by a block length; `process-refueling` did not, and ranks over the whole rate relation exactly as this does. Asserting BOTH counts is what makes the raggedness attributable: it is the rate and the ratio, not the cohort rule -- and 124 + 104 x 3 and 109 x 4 are the same 436, so the total alone would not say which.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rateSurvivorCount",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 436.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.run_chainedRowCount",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 312.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_survives",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 124
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_survives",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 164
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_outputOrdinal",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 105.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 124
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_outputOrdinal",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 164
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_activity_chain_reproduces_the_reference_source_hours",
