        {
          "id": "the_collapsed_base_rate_reproduces_the_reference_generator_table",
          "description": "`rtDay_meanBaseRate` IS `baseratebyage_1_2020.meanBaseRate` and `rtDay_meanBaseRateACAdj` IS its `meanBaseRateACAdj` -- the reference's own S14 intermediate, computed here from `emissionratebyage` and W and read from nothing. The table has 248 rows, 124 cohorts x 2 day types, which is the same 124 `pp_rateCohortCount` counts by a completely different route.\\n\\nThe A/C companion column is asserted beside the rate because it is exactly `rate x (fullACAdjustment - 1)` and the two would drift apart if the operating-mode weighting were applied to one and not the other. It is worth asserting even though `rt_acFactor` is 0 and it reaches no emitted number: this is the only place in the document where the A/C rows are checked at all.\\n\\nThe three species carry no rate: `emissionratebyage` has no 3201 row, so J22's inner join leaves rate_row 165 at the additive identity.",
